hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27990","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi: Malik, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad ibn Zurarah al-Ansariyyah, that she informed him, from Habibah bint Sahl al-Ansariyyah, she said: She was under Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out to dawn prayer and found Habibah bint Sahl at his door in the darkness. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Who is this. She said: I am Habibah bint Sahl. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is with you. She said: Neither I nor Thabit ibn Qays, to her husband. When Thabit came, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: This is Habibah bint Sahl; she mentioned what Allah willed to mention. Habibah said: O Messenger of Allah, all he gave me is with me. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Thabit: Take from her. So he took from her, and she sat among her family."
"27991","Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Harrani narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Umm Habibah bint Jahsh, that she had prolonged bleeding, and she asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he ordered her to wash at every prayer; though she would come out of the tub with the redness of blood over the water, then pray."
"27992","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Amrah, from Umm Habibah bint Jahsh, she said: I had prolonged bleeding for seven years, and I complained of that to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: That is not menstruation, but a vein, so wash. She used to wash at every prayer; she used to wash in the tub, and we would see the yellowness of blood in the tub."
